    delphi:hasConfidence "0.94"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "Under the standard meaning of computational universality, the conclusion follows directly from the definition and universal-machine theory. The qualification 'in a sense' matters, but the intended computational reading is explicit and checkable." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Formalize universality as effective emulation of any machine in a standard universal model. The emulator construction directly establishes that the system can realize behaviors of arbitrary computable complexity; a failure of the universality premise would refute the implication's application." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium> ;
